    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1143">

                <pb facs="1165" n="1151" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1151"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00/10–3144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-04T19:00:00-04:00">November 4, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>656. Most of the other American Republics have replied to the Department’s
                    circular telegram of October 31, 9 p.m. indicating willingness to extend early
                    recognition to the present régime in Guatemala. They have consequently been
                    informed that the United States will extend recognition at 5 p.m. Guatemala time
                    on Tuesday, November 7. At that time please deliver to the Government of
                    Guatemala an appropriate acknowledgment of its note of October 22, mentioned in
                    your telegram no. 711 of October 23, 5 p.m., expressing the desire of the
                    Government of the United States to maintain with the present Guatemalan
                    Administration, the warm friendship and the cordial cooperation which have so
                    happily characterized our relations with Guatemala in the past.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
